    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 93268 'Robgoblin Troublemakers!' (title), 103603 (card), objective 103600; icon 4540."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter: reference Npcs.json Id 4303 drawn at [-1495.18, -53.35, 930.89] (npc_spawns_extra.json spawn_guid 100000004303, FreeRealms-Legacy FabledRealms.lua). Region The Wilds, place Stillwater Crossing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 78 ('Robgoblin Troublemakers! (the live random encounter: robgoblin troublemakers and pranksters)'): scene sg_random_encounter_skullcamp, entry, exit, 3 waves, 10 spawns ({'Robgoblin Troublemaker': 5, 'Robgoblin Prankster': 5})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1241 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_skullcamp has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 30 coins / 140 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0136 (2026-11-11): model 4 robgoblin_m_basic.adr; the fight's waves field this kind, and 1914 sg_spawner_robgoblin_01.adr is the starter's junk-pile prop, not a fighter."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0136 (2026-11-11): this row is the battle's starter, the prop 2014 drew it as (the Snarler's den: video 5-IM2pBh2yY frames 01048 and 01080, red name, crossed swords, Press X; capture p12 t=546051.7 model 1938). The fight's own kind carries the body its waves fight with."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 prize wheel (2026-11-12): 'Robgoblin Troublemakers!' has no wheel of its own on the wiki; the wiki's item pages put its prize wheel with 'Den of Secrets' (Ninja's Blade of Flame Wave; Warrior’s Axe of Warcry; Wizard's Wand of Tsunami; Medic's Scalpel of Immunization), so it spins that wheel, from fandom 'Den of Secrets' (revision 49127), one per combat job, and 26 coins. The same pages also name Fleetfoot Ninja!, den_of_secrets, fleetfoot_ninja."
    }
  ]
